  "source_contracts": [
    {
      "contract": "Packed blocks are u, v, w, ph, t, mu. The legacy ru/rv/rw labels do not mean coupled momentum: first three blocks are velocity basis. Registry declares U/V as wind velocities; t is perturbation potential temperature and may be moist or dry depending on use_theta_m.",
      "source": "external/libtorch_wrf/sdirk3/wrf_sdirk3_state_layout.h:16-30,60-78,105-148; Registry/Registry.EM_COMMON:159-160,170-172,219-223",
      "topic": "packed prognostic vector order and basis"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Fortran serializes u then v then w then ph then t then mu, with i fastest, then k, then j; U uses x-staggered extent, V y-staggered, W/PH z-staggered. Solver dimensions are nx_u=nx+1, ny_v=ny+1, nz_w=nz+1 regardless of boundary flags.",
      "source": "external/libtorch_wrf/sdirk3/tests/native_terminal_adjoint_test.F:76-130,217-262; dyn_em/module_implicit_sdirk3.F:670-690,1428-1438",
      "topic": "Fortran pack order and native dimensions"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Mass owners end at min(ite,ide-1)/min(jte,jde-1); X-staggered U owns i through ite, Y-staggered V owns j through jte; vertical W/PH include nz_w. The specified local sample coordinates {2,6,10,14} avoid these upper owner boundaries for the current 17x17x16 native fixture. Three fields x 64 points x states 128 and 256 = 384 scalar samples.",
      "source": "external/libtorch_wrf/sdirk3/wrf_sdirk3_owned_box.h:8-22,65-95",
      "topic": "owner and sample validity"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Fortran passes whole-memory base pointers at ims/jms/kms; C++ adapts from memory origin to tile origin. Boundary flags (periodic, symmetric, open, specified, nested) are published separately at solver setup; do not infer ownership extents from periodicity.",
      "source": "external/libtorch_wrf/sdirk3/wrf_sdirk3_owned_box.h:8-22,45-61; dyn_em/module_implicit_sdirk3.F:730-744,1428-1441",
      "topic": "tile origin and boundary publication"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Native test prepare is guarded and runs after WRF initialization/CQ setup before the first advance; after-step capture runs on accepted internal endpoint before later physics/boundary processing. The current control_input64 hook is test-only at packed native entry; the accepted-state hook only captures the warm-prefix states it was designed for, so arbitrary twin controls/observations need an explicit later implementation decision.",
      "source": "dyn_em/solve_em.F:738-778; dyn_em/module_implicit_sdirk3.F:1428-1438; external/libtorch_wrf/sdirk3/wrf_sdirk3_tile_unified_impl.cpp:6100-6220,13097-13102",
      "topic": "test hook and caller timing"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Retained FP64 fixed-trajectory carry is mode 3 on one CPU tile covering the domain, rk_step 1, no split explicit/adaptive timestep, and rejects open, specified, nested, or polar boundaries. The code here does not establish which periodic setup the proposed experiment should choose.",
      "source": "external/libtorch_wrf/sdirk3/wrf_sdirk3_tile_unified_impl.cpp:6110-6190",
      "topic": "trajectory restrictions"
    }
  ],
